{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011NpJa6ATAnZQqEDnHDJnsp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WT899HikmyZyvGVsrcQWJc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/untestable.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_1\",\n    \"requirement\": \"you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'choose which card to cast' step requires the engine's player-choice API (controller.choose_card or similar) with a DeterministicPlayer decision. The test_utils API provides no way to pre-configure which card the player will pick when multiple instants/sorceries are in the graveyard. Tests can only verify that the chosen card left the graveyard, not that the full free-cast pipeline ran correctly.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A test helper such as `configure_player_choice(game, player_index, response)` that pre-loads the DeterministicPlayer's answer queue, or a `cast_from_graveyard(game, player_index, card_name)` utility that bypasses the choice prompt.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_1\",\n    \"requirement\": \"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"Fully verifying the exile-instead replacement requires the engine to (1) resolve the cast spell, (2) attempt to move it to the graveyard, and (3) apply the registered replacement that redirects it to exile. Steps 1 and 2 depend on the free-cast pipeline running fully (see previous entry). The existing test only checks the card is not in graveyard after the trigger effect runs, not that it specifically landed in exile.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"The same player-choice pre-loading helper described above, plus a test that resolves the stack (`game.stack.resolve_all()` or equivalent) and then checks `game.get_exile(p1).contains(the_cast_spell)`. The exile zone accessor already 