{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012Ff5m7m5pqZyNenmyLuAAE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LMtrUc8v2gm1fZnSwgRk9W","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/review.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1012,"cache_read_input_tokens":8533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1012,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DFXXYC7K6ejGetounKEpig","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"57c2aa60-df20-4c8a-a3cd-5e805837264e","request_id":"req_011CbUa7JeFUSWh4nPimJe1r","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer revision for sos_1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LMtrUc8v2gm1fZnSwgRk9W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 99,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"The _effect function does not actually cast the spell. It moves the card directly from graveyard to exile, completely bypassing the stack. According to the card's oracle text, the spell should be CAST without paying its mana cost, meaning it should go on the stack and can be countered, its on_resolve should fire, and it should produce its normal effect. The engine already provides cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD) for exactly this purpose (see cards/fdn/fdn_194/card_impl.py for precedent). Replace lines 99-106 with: `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` (wrapped in a try/except). Without this, the spell never resolves its effect, cannot be interacted with on the stack, and the entire 'cast from graveyard' mechanic is broken.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 93,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"The card text says 'you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard' — the cast is optional. The implementation unconditionally proceeds to move/cast the chosen spell with no yes/no prompt to the controller. A call to ctrl.choose_yes_no(...) is missing before selecting a candidate, allowing the player to decline. Without this, the controller is forced to always cast a spell when the trigger resolves, which is a rules violation.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 99,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"The exile-instead replacement effect is not implemented. The oracle text says 'If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.' This requires a replacement effect registered on the specific chosen card before it is cast, intercepting MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent and redirecting destination to exile. The current approach of manually moving to exile without casting means the replacement effect is irrelevant (nothing resolves through the normal pipeline), and the replacement contract from the spec is not fulfilled. After adopting cast_spell_free, a per-cast replacement effect must be registered on the chosen card using game.replacement_manager so that when _resolve_spell routes the non-permanent card to the graveyard the replacement redirects it to exile instead.\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n22\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n23\t    \"line\": 43,\n24\t    \"comment\": \"The supertypes merging pattern `(kwargs.get('supertypes') or set()) | {Supertype.LEGENDARY}` will fail with a TypeError if a caller passes supertypes as a set of plain strings (e.g. {'Legendary'}) rather than Supertype enum values, because set union of mixed string/enum types is silently wrong and the Supertype enum will not be recognised by the engine's equality checks. Etali (fdn_194) sets supertypes with a plain string set. While sos_1 itself sets the value correctly via setdefault, any downstream caller that reuses the pattern may hit this. Consider normalising string entries in the merge, or documenting that supertypes must be Supertype enum values.\"\n25\t  }\n26\t]\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DFXXYC7K6ejGetounKEpig","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"f776e33f-33fc-4a37-aa70-75c47395acbc","timestamp":"2026-05-28T07:27:50.438Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer revision for sos_1"}
