{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X4XrsR3WFS1NuJ21fM5fAb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Revised Implementation Rationale — SOS 1 The Dawning Archaic\n2\t\n3\t## Changes Made\n4\t\n5\t### Strict Issue 1: Use cast_spell_free instead of manual zone move\n6\t\n7\tThe trigger effect now calls `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` from\n8\t`engine/casting.py`. This places the chosen spell on the stack via the normal casting\n9\tpipeline, allowing it to be countered and have its effects resolve normally through\n10\t`on_resolve`. The old implementation manually moved the card from graveyard to exile,\n11\tbypassing the stack entirely.\n12\t\n13\t### Strict Issue 2: Optional cast (choose_yes_no prompt)\n14\t\n15\tAdded a `ctrl.choose_yes_no(...)` call before selecting a candidate. If the controller\n16\tdeclines (`False`), the effect returns early without casting anything. The call is\n17\twrapped in a try/except that defaults to `True` (yes) if no scripted answer is available,\n18\twhich ensures tests that don't script an answer still work correctly.\n19\t\n20\t### Strict Issue 3: Exile-instead replacement effect via game.replacement_manager\n21\t\n22\tTwo parts:\n23\t\n24\t1. **Engine change in `casting.py`'s `_resolve_spell`**: Before moving a resolved\n25\t   non-permanent (instant/sorcery) from the stack to the graveyard, the function now\n26\t   constructs a `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` with the card referenced as `card_obj`,\n27\t   applies `game.replacement_manager.apply()`, and routes the card to the zone specified\n28\t   by `destination` (either `\"graveyard\"` or `\"exile\"`). This is an additive change — it\n29\t   extends the existing resolution logic to honour replacement effects.\n30\t\n31\t2. **Card-level replacement in `card_impl.py`**: Before calling `cast_spell_free`, the\n32\t   trigger effect registers a `ReplacementEffect` on `game.replacement_manager` whose\n33\t   condition checks `event.card_obj is chosen_card`. When the chosen spell resolves and\n34\t   `_resolve_spell` consults the replacement manager, this replacement fires and sets\n35\t   `destination = \"exile\"`, redirecting the spell to exile instead of the graveyard.\n36\t\n37\t## Design Decisions\n38\t\n39\t- **`card_obj` attribute**: `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` has a `card` property that\n40\t  returns `None` for the base class (subclasses override it for creature/permanent death\n41\t  events). Rather than subclassing the event, I added a dynamic `card_obj` attribute on\n42\t  the event instance so conditions can match against the specific spell being resolved.\n43\t  This is a minimal, non-breaking addition.\n44\t\n45\t- **Fallback for choose_yes_no**: Tests use `DeterministicPlayer` with empty scripts.\n46\t  Wrapping in try/except and defaulting to `True` means tests that don't script the\n47\t  yes/no choice still pass (they implicitly assume the player always casts), matching\n48\t  the test's intent.\n49\t\n50\t- **Replacement cleanup on cast failure**: If `cast_spell_free` raises an exception (e.g.\n51\t  targeting fails), the registered replacement effect is cleaned up via\n52\t  `game.replacement_manager.unregister(chosen_card)` to avoid stale state.\n53\t\n54\t## No Disagreements\n55\t\n56\tAll three strict issues were valid and have been addressed. No disputes filed.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"6b8e39e9-76d7-49a2-bfb7-1b1270f3ee36","timestamp":"2026-05-28T07:31:03.092Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revised Implementation Rationale — SOS 1 The Dawning Archaic\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### Strict Issue 1: Use cast_spell_free instead of manual zone move\n\nThe trigger effect now calls `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` from\n`engine/casting.py`. This places the chosen spell on the stack via the normal casting\npipeline, allowing it to be countered and have its effects resolve normally through\n`on_resolve`. The old implementation manually moved the card from graveyard to exile,\nbypassing the stack entirely.\n\n### Strict Issue 2: Optional cast (choose_yes_no prompt)\n\nAdded a `ctrl.choose_yes_no(...)` call before selecting a candidate. If the controller\ndeclines (`False`), the effect returns early without casting anything. The call is\nwrapped in a try/except that defaults to `True` (yes) if no scripted answer is available,\nwhich ensures tests that don't script an answer still work correctly.\n\n### Strict Issue 3: Exile-instead replacement effect via game.replacement_manager\n\nTwo parts:\n\n1. **Engine change in `casting.py`'s `_resolve_spell`**: Before moving a resolved\n   non-permanent (instant/sorcery) from the stack to the graveyard, the function now\n   constructs a `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` with the card referenced as `card_obj`,\n   applies `game.replacement_manager.apply()`, and routes the card to the zone specified\n   by `destination` (either `\"graveyard\"` or `\"exile\"`). This is an additive change — it\n   extends the existing resolution logic to honour replacement effects.\n\n2. **Card-level replacement in `card_impl.py`**: Before calling `cast_spell_free`, the\n   trigger effect registers a `ReplacementEffect` on `game.replacement_manager` whose\n   condition checks `event.card_obj is chosen_card`. When the chosen spell resolves and\n   `_resolve_spell` consults the replacement manager, this replacement fires and sets\n   `destination = \"exile\"`, redirecting the spell to exile instead of the graveyard.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n- **`card_obj` attribute**: `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` has a `card` property that\n  returns `None` for the base class (subclasses override it for creature/permanent death\n  events). Rather than subclassing the event, I added a dynamic `card_obj` attribute on\n  the event instance so conditions can match against the specific spell being resolved.\n  This is a minimal, non-breaking addition.\n\n- **Fallback for choose_yes_no**: Tests use `DeterministicPlayer` with empty scripts.\n  Wrapping in try/except and defaulting to `True` means tests that don't script the\n  yes/no choice still pass (they implicitly assume the player always casts), matching\n  the test's intent.\n\n- **Replacement cleanup on cast failure**: If `cast_spell_free` raises an exception (e.g.\n  targeting fails), the registered replacement effect is cleaned up via\n  `game.replacement_manager.unregister(chosen_card)` to avoid stale state.\n\n## No Disagreements\n\nAll three strict issues were valid and have been addressed. No disputes filed.\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
