{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LsVvQn6Cm4XpL4UmfFdFnz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"1/1 white and black Inkling creature token\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine does not expose a public 'colors' attribute on tokens or on CardImpl instances in general. There is no ManaType-based color identity field on Creature tokens that is part of the standard API tested across all cards. Checking mana_cost on a token is not meaningful (tokens have no mana cost).\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Add a 'colors' set attribute (e.g. {Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK}) to CardImpl or Creature that is set during token creation; or document that token colors are encoded in a specific attribute the Implementer must set, so a test can assert it.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"you may cast a copy of its spell (Swords to Plowshares)\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The mechanic says the card 'becomes prepared' and you 'may cast a copy'. The exact public API for triggering/casting the copy (e.g. whether it goes on the stack, uses cast_spell_free, or is invoked via a special method) is not defined by the engine or prior KEY_DECISIONS. Tests call cast_prepared_spell() directly as the expected surface; if the Implementer uses a different method name or routes through an activated ability, the test will need renaming but the behavioral contract is still clear.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Specify in KEY_DECISIONS whether 'cast copy while prepared' uses an ActivatedAbility (discoverable via get_activated_abilities()), a dedicated cast_prepared_spell() method, or some other hook. This would let the test call the correct API rather than assuming a method name.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"ecc48a40-f74a-48a5-98f7-bda7d37dc94d","