{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MvSAqpTamWFQJk5dJWkvB6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 131,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"cast_prepared_spell reads `base_power` to determine life gained, but Swords to Plowshares grants life equal to the creature's current power (rule 701.13a). For a creature with +1/+1 or -1/-1 counters, `base_power` will be wrong. The `Creature` class exposes a `power` property (modified_power + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters) that reflects the correct in-game value. Change to: `power = getattr(target_creature, 'power', getattr(target_creature, 'base_power', 0))`.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 80,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"The Inkling token is constructed without color information. The card spec specifies it is a '1/1 white and black Inkling creature token'. The `Creature` base class derives color from `mana_cost`; with no mana cost set the token is effectively colorless. If the engine ever checks token colors (e.g. for protection from white/black), this will produce wrong results. Consider adding a `colors` attribute or a mana_cost placeholder if the engine supports it.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 149,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"The life-gain guard `if target_controller is not None and power > 0` skips firing `GainsLifeTriggeredEvent` when the exiled creature has 0 power. Per the rules, Swords to Plowshares causes the player to 'gain 0 life', which is a no-op but technically should still be an event. Downstream triggers that watch GainsLifeTriggeredEvent for any amount would miss the event. Low risk in practice but worth noting.\"\n19\t  }\n20\t]\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgzLdpMVt