{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_013kWDdFwRDS4b42eahcVoGJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013xe8YsVB3nen2KkFHvTkun","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale: Mana Sculpt (sos_57)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### 1. BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (engine/events.py)\nAdded a new dataclass `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with two fields:\n- `active_player`: the player whose main phase it is (used for the condition check)\n- `phase`: which main phase (PRECOMBAT_MAIN or POSTCOMBAT_MAIN)\n\nThis is purely additive — no existing events were renamed or removed.\n\n### 2. Firing the event in engine/turn.py\nAdded firing of `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` at the start of both `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` and `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` phases in `run_turn()`. This is consistent with how `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` is fired at UPKEEP. The event fires before priority is given, so delayed mana triggers will correctly be placed on the stack at the very start of the main phase.\n\n### 3. ManaSculpt class\n- Inherits from `Instant` (not just `CardImpl`) to ensure `CardType.INSTANT` is in `card_types`\n- `get_targets()` returns a single `TargetRequirement` with `zone=Zone.STACK` and a permissive filter (any stack object)\n- `on_resolve()`:\n  1. Gets chosen target from `self.chosen_targets`\n  2. Records the CMC of the countered spell's source card's mana cost before removing it\n  3. Removes the target from the stack via list comprehension on `game.stack._items` (identity-based, additive-safe)\n  4. Checks if controller has a Wizard on their battlefield only\n  5. If yes, registers a `TriggerRegistration` for `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` with a condition that only fires for the controller's main phase\n\n### 4. One-shot trigger pattern\nThe delayed trigger calls `game.trigger_manager.unregister(source)` inside its effect to clean up after firing. The source used for the trigger is `self` (the ManaSculpt card instance), ensuring identity-based unregistration only removes this specific trigger.\n\n### 5. Stack counter implementation\nUsed `game.stack._items = [item for item in game.stack._items if item is not target]` instead of `game.stack.pop()` because the countered spell may not be on top of the stack (other spells may have been cast in response). This correctly removes only the targeted spell while leaving others intact.\n\n## Conventions Established\n- `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` fires at the start of BOTH main phases, allowing cards to check `event.active_player` to determine if it's their phase\n- Delayed one-shot triggers self-unregister via `game.trigger_manager.unregister(source)` in their effect\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":123,"cache_read_input_tokens":53855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":123,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011xz6oLC5Frvp92ie79V1tq","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"7b31a6e2-20e6-4480-86dd-a23754639c38","request_id":"req_011CbUcB5tdWM4NUhpeWCy4C","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_57"}
