{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_018oS73891MEmDAeiBh3a522","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PNxCSJQKmsS6mVQaXCBs8t","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n\n## File: cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py\n\n### TestRalZarekGuestLecturerProperties — Static card properties\n\nThese tests verify the fundamental, invariant card data that any correct\nimplementation must expose from `__init__`:\n\n- **test_name**: name attribute equals \"Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\".\n- **test_mana_cost**: mana_cost parses to `{1}{B}{B}`.\n- **test_is_planeswalker**: isinstance check against `Planeswalker` base class; `CardType.PLANESWALKER` in `card_types`.\n- **test_ral_subtype**: \"Ral\" is in `subtypes` (the Planeswalker subtype from `type_line`).\n- **test_legendary_supertype**: `Supertype.LEGENDARY` in `supertypes`.\n- **test_starting_loyalty_three**: `starting_loyalty == 3` (printed on the card).\n- **test_initial_loyalty_equals_starting**: `loyalty == starting_loyalty` immediately after construction.\n- **test_exposes_loyalty_abilities**: `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns a list of exactly 4 entries (+1, -1, -2, -7).\n- **test_loyalty_ability_types**: Every entry in that list is a `LoyaltyAbility` instance.\n- **test_ability_loyalty_costs**: The costs +1, -1, -2, -7 are all present among the returned abilities.\n\n### TestRalZarekPlusOneAbility — +1: Surveil 2\n\n- **test_plus1_increases_loyalty_from_3_to_4**: activating the +1 ability increments loyalty by 1.\n- **test_plus1_surveil_sends_top_card_to_graveyard_when_scripted_yes**: with scripts `[True, True]`, both top 2 library cards move to the graveyard.\n- **test_plus1_surveil_keeps_card_on_library_when_scripted_no**: with scripts `[False, False]`, neither card leaves the library.\n- **test_plus1_surveil_partial_send_to_graveyard**: with scripts `[True, False]`, exactly one of the two cards enters the graveyard.\n- **test_plus1_surveil_empty_library_does_not_raise**: with an empty library, surveil 2 is a no-op and loyalty still increments.\n\nEdge cases covered:\n- Single-card library (handled by min(2, len) logic) — implicit in the partial test.\n- Empty library — explicit test.\n\n### TestRalZarekMinusOneAbility — -1: Any number of target players each discard\n\n- **test_minus1_decreases_loyalty_from_3_to_2**: loyalty changes from 3 → 2.\n- **test_minus1_targeted_player_discards_one_card**: the targeted player's hand shrinks by 1 and the card appears in their graveyard.\n- **test_minus1_with_no_targets_is_a_noop**: with `chosen_targets = []`, the ability resolves without crashing.\n- **test_minus1_multiple_players_each_discard**: when both players are targeted, each discards a card.\n\nThe \"any number\" wording means 0 targets must be allowed; a no-targets test is included.\n\n### TestRalZarekMinusTwoAbility — -2: Reanimate creature with MV ≤ 3\n\n- **test_minus2_decreases_loyalty_from_3_to_1**: loyalty changes from 3 → 1.\n- **test_minus2_returns_mv3_creature_to_battlefield**: a creature at MV 3 (the boundary) enters the battlefield.\n- **test_minus2_returns_mv1_creature_to_battlefield**: a creature at MV 1 also qualifies.\n- **test_minus2_does_not_return_mv4_creature**: MV 4 is exactly one above the limit; if set as chosen target the card remains in the graveyard.\n- **test_minus2_does_not_return_mv5_creature**: additional over-limit check at MV 5.\n- **test_minus2_with_no_target_does_not_raise**: with `chosen_targets = []`, no exception is thrown.\n\nThe \"from your graveyard\" restriction means the card must come from the controller's graveyard; tests set up the graveyard via `set_board_state` which assigns ownership to the player, matching this contract.\n\n### TestRalZarekMinusSevenAbility — -7: Flip five coins, skip X turns\n\n- **test_minus7_correct_loyalty_cost**: verifies the ability at index 3 has `loyalty_cost == -7`.\n- **test_minus7_loyalty_adjustment**: with inflated loyalty (7), after activation loyalty becomes 0.\n- **test_minus7_all_heads_skips_five_turns**: patches `random.random` to return 0.0 (heads) for all 5 flips; asserts `p2.turns_to_skip == 5`.\n- **test_minus7_all_tails_skips_zero_turns**: patches to always return tails; asserts `p2.turns_to_skip == 0`.\n\nEdge cases NOT covered (and why):\n- Mixed coin results (e.g. 3 heads out of 5): the all-heads and all-tails tests establish the counting\n  contract; intermediate values are implied and would require exact mock sequencing that is fragile.\n- \"Skips their next X turns\" interaction with the extra-turns queue: the engine's turn-skipping\n  mechanism (`turns_to_skip` vs. `extra_turns`) is the Implementer's choice; the test checks the\n  most natural attribute name and is recorded in `untestable.json` for the corner case.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5577,"cache_read_input_tokens":48336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5577,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018AjBE3qG9KbaA4TaNnugLh","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"e3aeb037-bfee-4108-9ebc-df0ab4cf6769","request_id":"req_011CbUccnc3geCxHu9yRq9AN","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Tester for sos_97"}
