{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159KRHLChoaCgamWgNoqps4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator Directives for sos_97\n2\t\n3\t## Untestable Requirement: Turn skip (-7 ability)\n4\t\n5\tThe Tester could not verify turn-skip state because the engine lacks a standard `turns_to_skip` attribute on players.\n6\t\n7\tPlease:\n8\t1. Add `turns_to_skip: int = 0` to the Player class in `engine/player.py` (additive only)\n9\t2. Use this attribute in the -7 ability implementation\n10\t3. Use `random.random()` (not `random.choice`, `random.randint`, etc.) for coin flips so tests can patch it with `unittest.mock.patch('random.random')`\n11\t\n12\t## Surveil 2 (+1 ability)\n13\t\n14\tSurveil 2: Look at the top 2 cards of your library; put any number into your graveyard and the rest on top in any order.\n15\t- Implementation should move the looked-at cards: some to graveyard, some back to top of library\n16\t- The choice of which cards go where is controlled by the player's choice mechanism\n17\t\n18\t## Note on -1 discard\n19\t\n20\tUse `player.choose_card(hand_cards)` (or whichever method matches DeterministicPlayer's script) to select a card to discard. Ensure the discard order matches what DeterministicPlayer expects.\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015Xrzn5FfvWU8rwgUW3kSyV","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"57756d61-58d1-4e5a-91f7-844a1227303f","timestamp":"2026-05-28T08:02:49.290Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_97"}
