mpl.py\",\n23\t    \"line\": 149,\n24\t    \"comment\": \"The -7 coin flip uses bare random.random() (Python stdlib) rather than any deterministic game-level RNG. While the tests correctly mock random.random at the module level and it works, for reproducibility and testability it would be preferable to route through a game-level source of randomness if one exists in the engine.\"\n25\t  },\n26\t  {\n27\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n28\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\",\n29\t    \"line\": 82,\n30\t    \"comment\": \"Surveil: the comment on line 81 says 'keep them in the same relative order (bottom-to-top)', but the actual ordering policy for kept cards in the official Surveil rules is that the player may arrange them in any order they choose. The implementation silently preserves the original relative order rather than prompting the player to choose an order. This is a rules fidelity issue but marked advisory since the tests do not cover reordering.\"\n31\t  }\n32\t]\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0123C2BZbXrQpq57qgUa3F9h","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"d4b8bd3a-e9e0-4abd-8afa-1b46ec37569a","timestamp":"2026-05-28T08:07:25.248Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer revision for sos_97"}
