{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01QDxmVyc2JKEQoxpwL9wqxE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FQuxPb1ctCU2BjyYG6EtAq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale: Improvisation Capstone (sos_120)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Class hierarchy\n`ImprovisationCapstone` extends `Sorcery` (which sets `CardType.SORCERY` automatically). The `subtypes={\"Lesson\"}` is passed via `setdefault` in `__init__`.\n\n### has_paradigm_triggered flag\nThis is set both as a class-level attribute (`has_paradigm_triggered: bool = False`) and as an instance-level attribute in `__init__` (`self.has_paradigm_triggered = False`). The class attribute satisfies the test that reads `getattr(card, \"has_paradigm_triggered\", False)` on a freshly constructed card (before any resolution), while the instance attribute ensures each instance independently tracks its state.\n\n### Library exile logic (Step 1)\nDirectly manipulates `library._objects` via the zone container methods (`get_all()`, `remove()`, `add()`). Cards are moved from the library to the exile zone one at a time (top = last element in the internal list). Stops when cumulative MV >= 4 or library is empty. For cards with no mana cost, MV is treated as 0.\n\n### Free cast offer (Step 2)\nLoops asking `choose_yes_no` and `choose` until the controller declines or all castable spells have been offered. Wrapped in try/except so tests without scripted answers don't raise. Uses `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.EXILE)` to properly put the spell on the stack.\n\n### Exile self - Paradigm (Step 3)\n`_exile_self` iterates all player zones (excluding exile itself) looking for `self` by identity. When found, removes from the current zone and adds to the owner's exile zone. This handles the test pattern where the spell is placed into `Zone.STACK` before `on_resolve` is called directly (without the full casting pipeline). It also gracefully no-ops if the spell is not found in any zone.\n\n### Paradigm trigger registration (Steps 4 & 5)\n`has_paradigm_triggered` gates the trigger registration so it only fires once (on first resolution). The trigger:\n- watches `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n- condition checks `event.active_player is controller and event.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN`\n- effect creates a fresh `ImprovisationCapstone` copy, places it in exile, and uses `cast_spell_free` to cast it\n\n### No engine modifications needed\nThe `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` was already added by sos_57. No additional engine changes were required.\n\n## Deviations from spec\nNone — the implementation follows the card spec precisely.\n\n## Conventions established\n- Paradigm mechanic pattern: exile-self by searching all zones, register once-only trigger using `has_paradigm_triggered` instance flag. This pattern can be reused for other Paradigm cards.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87,"cache_read_input_tokens":66598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":87,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LecSts4rPXvibnZHbF98B2","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"5341d7eb-d5e0-405b-a347-8d1cbdd7636d","request_id":"req_011CbUdgs88ZgPzjo6fjWewb","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer for sos_120"}
