{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CyARviaPZPupZEBNtgtPZ1","type":"tool_result","content":"340\t    def power(self) -> int:\n341\t        \"\"\"Current power including counter modifications.\"\"\"\n342\t        return self.modified_power + self.plus_one_counters - self.minus_one_counters\n343\t\n344\t    @property\n345\t    def toughness(self) -> int:\n346\t        \"\"\"Current toughness including counter modifications.\"\"\"\n347\t        return self.modified_toughness + self.plus_one_counters - self.minus_one_counters\n348\t\n349\t\n350\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n351\t# Instant / Sorcery\n352\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n353\t\n354\tclass Instant(CardImpl):\n355\t    \"\"\"An instant spell — no extra fields beyond CardImpl.\"\"\"\n356\t\n357\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n358\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.INSTANT}\n359\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n360\t\n361\t\n362\tclass Sorcery(CardImpl):\n363\t    \"\"\"A sorcery spell — no extra fields beyond CardImpl.\"\"\"\n364\t\n365\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n366\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.SORCERY}\n367\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n368\t\n369\t\n370\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n371\t# Enchantment\n372\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n373\t\n374\tclass Enchantment(CardImpl):\n375\t    \"\"\"An enchantment card.\n376\t\n377\t    For auras, use the :class:`Aura` subclass which sets ``is_aura = True``.\n378\t    The base ``Enchantment`` class retains the ``attached_to`` attribute for\n379\t    backwards compatibility but marks ``is_aura = False`` so that state-based\n380\t    actions do not treat a non-aura enchantment as an unattached aura.\n381\t\n382\t    Attributes:\n383\t        attached_to: The object this enchantment is attached to (``None``\n384\t            if not an aura or not yet attached).\n385\t        is_aura: ``False`` for regular enchantments; ``True`` for auras.\n386\t    \"\"\"\n387\t\n388\t    is_aura: bool = False\n389\t\n390\t    def __init__(self, attached_to: Any | None = None, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n391\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.ENCHANTMENT}\n392\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n393\t        self.attached_to: Any | None = attached_to\n394\t\n395\t    def apply_continuous_effect(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n396\t        \"\"\"Apply the enchantment's continuous effect to the game.\"\"\"\n397\t\n398\t    def on_enchant(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n399\t        \"\"\"Called when this enchantment becomes attached to an object.\"\"\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012Bcc4JYG6hJa8Trzue8gF3","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"b2bc0282-660e-4381-836c-012135fa881b","timestamp":"2026-05-28T08:16:09.106Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Reviewer for sos_120"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a8037fd28ef5c2862","tool_use_id":"toolu_012Bcc4JYG6hJa8Trzue8gF3","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":46443,"tool_uses":19,"duration_ms":66890},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"aa854c1b-7de8-40e8-aaf2-c318ec81cabb","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011PywhAbWrUv52vqRqpUAz5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjsNybxjAv9Ep4zveC5UrZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 81,\n    \"comment\": \"The library-exile loop exits as soon as total_mv < 4 is false, meaning it stops once total_mv reaches exactly 4. However, zero-CMC cards (e.g. lands accidentally reaching this code path, or 0-cost spells) will be added to exiled_cards and increment total_mv by 0, creating an infinite loop when the library contains only 0-MV cards. The loop condition `while total_mv < 4` never becomes false when no card provides any MV, so the loop runs until the library is completely exhausted. This is arguably correct MTG rules behaviour (exile all cards until threshold met or library empty) but is worth noting. More critically: if a library has only 0-MV non-land cards, the entire library is exiled — this is correct per rules but the implementation should not be confused with the infinite-loop guard. The real bug here is the comment on line 85 saying 'Top of library is last in the list (index -1)' — but the code calls `lib_objects[-1]` AFTER calling `library.get_all()` which returns a snapshot. After each `library.remove(top_card)`, `lib_objects` is stale and still contains the old top. The next iteration calls `lib_objects = library.get_all()` again at the top of the while loop, so the loop correctly refreshes the snapshot each iteration. This is fine. No bug here.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 103,\n    \"comment\": \"The Paradigm trigger registration guard `if not self.has_paradigm_triggered` fires before `self.has_paradigm_triggered = True` is set. This means that on EVERY call to on_resolve (e.g. the copy cast each main phase also resolves and calls on_resolve), a new trigger registration is added to the TriggerManager if the specific instance has not already triggered. Because each copy created in _effect() is a fresh ImprovisationCapstone() instance with has_paradigm_triggered=False, every time the Paradigm copy resolves it will register ANOTHER recurring trigger. Each additional resolution of a copy snowballs the trigger count unboundedly. The intent per the spec is that the recurring trigger is registered only the FIRST time any spell with this name resolves for the controller — this is a per-controller/game-name flag, not a per-instance flag. The instance-level flag cannot guard against multiple copies resolving. A shared game-level flag (e.g. stored on the game state or on the controller) keyed by card name and controller is needed.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 167,\n    \"comment\": \"_exile_self iterates over all zones of all players to find `self` and move it to `owner.zones[Zone.EXILE]`. However, the destination is always routed to `owner`'s exile zone (computed from `getattr(self, 'owner', controller)`). When Improvisation Capstone is cast by a player who is not the owner (e.g. stolen/copied), the card would be exiled to the wrong player's exile zone. Per MTG rules, exiling goes to the owner's exile zone, so this is technically correct, but more importantly the comment says 'owner = getattr(self, 'owner', controller) or controller' which falls back to controller. If controller and owner differ, the card goes to owner exile which is correct but the fallback `or controller` would send it to controller exile if owner is None — this is the same issue as before. This is a minor edge case for the test harness, but it is an inconsistency worth flagging.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 228,\n    \"comment\": \"The _effect closure inside _register_paradigm_trigger creates a fresh ImprovisationCapstone copy and adds it to the controller's exile zone, then casts it free from exile. When this copy resolves (on_resolve is called), it will: (1) attempt to exile cards from the library again, (2) call _exile_self which will move itself to exile, and (3) because has_paradigm_triggered is False on the new copy instance, it will call _register_paradigm_trigger AGAIN, registering yet another BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent trigger. This causes unbounded accumulation of triggers with each subsequent Paradigm copy resolution — a functional bug. The fix is to track the paradigm state at the game/controller level rather than per instance.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 38,\n    \"comment\": \"Class-level `has_paradigm_triggered: bool = False` is declared as a class attribute, then overridden as an instance attribute in __init__. The class-level declaration is misleading since it creates a shared class attribute that is immediately shadowed for every instance. Only the instance attribute (set in __init__) matters. The class-level declaration can be removed to avoid confusion.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 163,\n    \"comment\": \"The `except Exception: pass` swallowing in _offer_free_casts (line 163-164) silently drops all errors from cast_spell_free, including CastingErrors that might indicate genuine bugs (e.g. card not found in exile because _exile_self already moved it). At minimum the exception should be logged or re-raised as a best-effort. In the test harness this makes failures invisible.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 175,\n    \"comment\": \"In _exile_self, iterating `for zone in Zone` includes Zone.STACK. During on_resolve, the card IS typically on the stack (moved there during casting). The code skips Zone.EXILE but not Zone.STACK — this is correct since the card should be found in Zone.STACK and moved to exile. However, if called outside of the casting pipeline (direct on_resolve call without going through cast_spell / cast_spell_free), the card will not be in any zone and _exile_self becomes a no-op, which is acceptable per the comment but slightly fragile. The test at line 294 in tests.py explicitly places the card in Zone.STACK before calling on_resolve to validate this path.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":863,"cache_read_input_tokens":45108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":863,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012Bcc4JYG6hJa8Trzue8gF3","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"101cb089-3d01-4346-9b11-5c3f1e662b0c","request_id":"req_011CbUdoBUMcc2K4rSfhMg2k","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Reviewer for sos_120"}
