{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_014p8mkDn2NRLvbo3rtGv3os","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fotq7gMjHGPKMz2jrk9EQE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision Rationale — Improvisation Capstone (SOS 120)\n\n## Strict Issues Fixed\n\n### Issue 1: Game-scoped trigger registration guard\n\nThe original code used `self.has_paradigm_triggered` as the guard. Every new\n`ImprovisationCapstone` instance created by the Paradigm copy mechanism starts\nwith `has_paradigm_triggered = False`, so each copy resolution would register\nyet another `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger — unbounded accumulation.\n\n**Fix:** Added `paradigm_registered: set[tuple[int, str]]` to `GameState.__init__`\n(additive-only engine change). The set stores `(id(controller), card.name)` tuples.\nIn `on_resolve`, the trigger is registered only when the key is absent from that set.\n\nThe per-instance `has_paradigm_triggered` attribute is retained unchanged because\nthe test contract requires it to be `False` on fresh instances and `True` after\n`on_resolve` returns.\n\n### Issue 2: Paradigm copies re-registering triggers\n\nWhen the Paradigm trigger fires, it creates a new `ImprovisationCapstone` copy and\ncasts it for free. When that copy resolves, its `on_resolve` would (under the old\ncode) also pass the instance-level guard and register another trigger.\n\n**Fix:** Added `is_paradigm_copy: bool = False` instance attribute. When the\n`_effect` closure creates a copy it sets `copy.is_paradigm_copy = True`. In\n`on_resolve`, the `should_register` check combines two guards:\n\n```python\nshould_register = (\n    not self.is_paradigm_copy\n    and _key not in game.paradigm_registered\n)\n```\n\nThis means a Paradigm copy can never register a trigger regardless of the\ngame-scoped set state.\n\n## Advisory Issues (acknowledged, not acted on)\n\n- **Class-level `has_paradigm_triggered` annotation** (line 38 original): removed\n  the class-level annotation; the instance attribute in `__init__` is the only one.\n- **Silent `except Exception: pass` in `_offer_free_casts`**: removed the bare\n  `pass` — the `cast_spell_free` call is now unguarded so failures propagate. The\n  outer catch-all that exited on `choose_yes_no` failure was already appropriate\n  (avoids infinite loop on tests without scripted answers).\n\n## Conventions established\n\n- `game.paradigm_registered` is a `set[tuple[int, str]]` keyed by\n  `(id(controller), card_name)` for per-controller Paradigm deduplication.\n- Paradigm copy objects carry `is_paradigm_copy = True` as a lightweight marker\n  that suppresses trigger re-registration without further game-state lookups.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135,"cache_read_input_tokens":31610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":135,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":55,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QH1fmdpWpKvYErs3r38Nv7","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"ca14b439-282b-4a32-88a4-41fa547e46de","request_id":"req_011CbUdyrMTxe6MhvpeVJDUH","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implementer revision for sos_120"}
