{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QH1fmdpWpKvYErs3r38Nv7","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 28 tests pass.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/disagreements.json\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **`engine/game_state.py`** — Added `self.paradigm_registered: set[tuple[int, str]] = set()` to `GameState.__init__`. This game-scoped set tracks `(id(controller), card_name)` tuples of controllers whose Paradigm trigger has been registered, preventing duplicate trigger accumulation across all instances.\n\n2. **`cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py`** — Three changes:\n   - Added `self.is_paradigm_copy: bool = False` instance attribute. The `_effect` closure sets `copy.is_paradigm_copy = True` before casting the Paradigm copy. `on_resolve` skips trigger registration when this flag is set.\n   - Replaced the per-instance `has_paradigm_triggered` guard with a dual guard: `not self.is_paradigm_copy and _key not in game.paradigm_registered`. The per-instance flag is retained for test contract compatibility.\n   - Removed the silent `except Exception: pass` around `cast_spell_free` in `_offer_free_casts` (advisory fix)."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acd38bec9642ae015 (use SendMessage with to: 'acd38bec9642ae015' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 35183\ntool_uses: 22\nduration_ms: 125636</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"3ef50069-88e7-48c8-8f5d-74f2969d1ce0","timestamp":"2026-05-28T08:19:23.559Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Revise the implementation of SOS card sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone) to address strict reviewer comments.\n\nImplementation file: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\nTests file: /workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py (DO NOT MODIFY)\nReview comments: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json\nFILES_MODIFIED.json: /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json\nKEY_DECISIONS.md: /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md\n\nSTRICT ISSUES TO FIX:\n\n1. (line ~103) The Paradigm trigger registration guard uses a per-instance flag (`self.has_paradigm_triggered`). Copies created by the paradigm mechanism each start with `has_paradigm_triggered = False`, so each copy resolution registers ANOTHER trigger. Fix: use a game-scoped or controller-scoped flag keyed by card name (e.g., store in `game.state_flags` or `controller.paradigm_triggered_cards` as a set of card names). The flag must be checked/set in a way that persists across all instances of this card name.\n\n2. (line ~228) The paradigm copy should NOT repeat the main effect (exiling from library) when it resolves. The copy represents casting the Sorcery again, but for Paradigm purposes the copy should execute the main effect (exile from library and free casts) but NOT call _register_paradigm_trigger again (since the persistent trigger is already registered). The easiest fix: mark copies with a flag (e.g., `is_paradigm_copy = True`) and in on_resolve, skip the paradigm trigger registration if is_paradigm_copy is True.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION APPROACH:\n- Add a game-state-level tracking dictionary (e.g., use `game.paradigm_registered` as a set of card names that have registered their paradigm trigger)\n- In on_resolve: if card name not in game.paradigm_registered → register trigger, add name to game.paradigm_registered\n- When creating a paradigm copy: set `is_paradigm_copy = True` on the copy\n- In on_resolve: if `is_paradigm_copy` is True → skip paradigm trigger registration\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n- Apply ALL strict review comments.\n- Do NOT modify the test file.\n- Run tests to verify all 28 tests still pass.\n- Write output to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised.diff, impl-revised-rationale.md\n- Update FILES_MODIFIED.json entry for sos_120 in place.\n\nReturn:\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: N\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-