{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BSUeMmJArj5b3LwX7EUCDL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KRZCj3k9H55SUkzfj8S5gm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant\n\n## File: cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py\n\n### TestSilverquillStaticProperties (11 tests)\n\nVerifies every static property from the card spec:\n\n- `test_name` — card name matches spec exactly.\n- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` subclass and has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n- `test_mana_cost` — full mana cost `{2}{W}{B}` parses correctly.\n- `test_mana_cost_contains_white_pip` — white pip present in cost (color identity).\n- `test_mana_cost_contains_black_pip` — black pip present in cost (color identity).\n- `test_base_power` — printed power is 4.\n- `test_base_toughness` — printed toughness is 4.\n- `test_has_flying` — `Keyword.FLYING` is in the keyword flags.\n- `test_has_vigilance` — `Keyword.VIGILANCE` is in the keyword flags.\n- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` is in supertypes.\n- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include both \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\".\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyGrantAPI (2 tests)\n\nVerifies the public API for the casualty grant exists:\n\n- `test_has_get_casualty_value_method` — the method must exist.\n- `test_get_casualty_value_callable` — it must be callable.\n\nModeled after the miracle API pattern in sos_201 (`get_miracle_cost`).\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyGrantValue (5 tests)\n\nVerifies the casualty 1 grant returns the correct value for the right spell types:\n\n- `test_instant_gets_casualty_value_one` — instants owned by controller get casualty 1.\n- `test_sorcery_gets_casualty_value_one` — sorceries owned by controller get casualty 1.\n- `test_creature_does_not_get_casualty` — creature cards return None/falsy.\n- `test_opponent_instant_does_not_get_casualty` — opponent's cards return None/falsy (only \"you\" benefit).\n- `test_uncontrolled_silverquill_returns_none` — no controller means no grant (guard pattern from KEY_DECISIONS.md sos_201).\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyCopyMechanic (7 tests)\n\nVerifies the casualty sacrifice-and-copy mechanic:\n\n- `test_casting_instant_with_casualty_creates_copy_on_stack` — when player opts in and sacrifices a power >= 1 creature, a copy is pushed onto the stack.\n- `test_casualty_creature_leaves_battlefield` — the sacrificed creature is removed from the battlefield.\n- `test_casualty_sacrificed_creature_goes_to_graveyard` — the sacrificed creature ends up in the graveyard.\n- `test_declining_casualty_does_not_create_copy` — if player says \"no\" to the sacrifice prompt, no copy is created.\n- `test_no_casualty_when_no_eligible_creature` — a 0-power creature is not eligible; no copy is created even if player answers \"yes\".\n- `test_creature_with_power_ge_1_is_eligible_for_casualty` — power exactly 1 meets the casualty 1 threshold.\n- `test_casualty_does_not_fire_for_non_instant_sorcery` — the casualty hook is a no-op for non-instant/sorcery card types (e.g., creatures).\n\n## Edge Cases Covered\n\n- The \"only your spells\" restriction (opponent's cards not affected).\n- The \"controller is None\" guard (mirrors the sos_201 miracle pattern).\n- Power == 0 is NOT eligible; power == 1 IS eligible (exact boundary).\n- Declining means no copy and no sacrifice.\n- Casualty only applies to instants and sorceries, not all spell types.\n\n## Edge Cases NOT Covered\n\n- Choosing new targets on the copy: the engine's `copy_spell` in `stack.py` supports\n  `new_targets`, but the test harness has no scripted target-selection surface for\n  casualty copies. This is tracked in `untestable.json`.\n- The copy resolving and producing its effect independently of the original: verifying\n  that both the original spell and its copy fully resolve would require a targeted\n  instant/sorcery with observable effects and target-scripting support. Tracked in `untestable.json`.\n- Interaction with multiple Silverquills: not required by the spec.\n- Silverquill attacking without tapping (vigilance combat behavior): covered by the\n  engine's existing combat tests; not re-tested here.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4616,"cache_read_input_tokens":56601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4616,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4fNW57avaPadQXpKSq7YV","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"f4b450b4-221d-4473-bd3c-a90b04e46270","request_id":"req_011CbUfYBd6xBJnfutbKFh54","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Tester for sos_226"}
