{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fgerequ9qxd5J2TVXmtMNu","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 25 tests pass.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/disagreements.json\n\n**Summary of changes made:**\n\n1. **`engine/casting.py`** — Added `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` import and fired `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` at the end of `cast_spell()` (after the StackObject is pushed). This is an additive-only change that integrates spell-cast event signaling into the casting pipeline.\n\n2. **`cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`** — Three strict fixes applied:\n   - **Controller fix**: `ctrl = spell.controller` with explicit `None` return (no silent fallback), plus explicit `ctrl is not self.controller` check to reject opponent spells.\n   - **copy_spell fix**: Replaced `copy.copy(spell)` with `copy_spell(game, temp_stack_obj, ctrl)` from `engine/stack.py` to avoid shared mutable state. A temporary `StackObject` wraps the spell card to satisfy `copy_spell`'s API.\n   - **Casting pipeline hook**: `register_triggers()` now registers a `TriggerRegistration` for `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`. The `_condition` captures the matched spell in a `_pending` list; `_effect` pops it and calls `_apply_casualty_for_spell`. This connects Silverquill's casualty mechanic to actual gameplay.\n   - **Exception handling**: Changed `except (ScriptExhaustedError, Exception)` to `except ScriptExhaustedError` so real bugs surface."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: abba2751bb2a93457 (use SendMessage with to: 'abba2751bb2a93457' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 61406\ntool_uses: 41\nduration_ms: 252917</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"b79c6f6f-1b19-449d-98c3-666da9c22fac","timestamp":"2026-05-28T08:48:24.864Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Revise t