{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_019RkQFhUdaSYMLDL7BqVc7W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AVTFnbNLZbaVKsTjSinw6S","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — SOS 245: Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n\n### Class: `TestWitherbloomStaticProperties`\n\nTests that the card's static metadata matches the spec exactly.\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|---|---|\n| `test_name` | Card name is \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\" |\n| `test_is_creature` | Instance of `Creature`; `CardType.CREATURE` in `card_types` |\n| `test_mana_cost` | Full mana cost parses to `{6}{B}{G}` |\n| `test_mana_cost_contains_black_pip` | Black mana pip present |\n| `test_mana_cost_contains_green_pip` | Green mana pip present |\n| `test_base_power` | Printed power is 5 |\n| `test_base_toughness` | Printed toughness is 5 |\n| `test_has_flying` | `Keyword.FLYING` in keywords |\n| `test_has_deathtouch` | `Keyword.DEATHTOUCH` in keywords |\n| `test_is_legendary` | `Supertype.LEGENDARY` in supertypes |\n| `test_is_elder_dragon` | Both \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\" in subtypes |\n\n---\n\n### Class: `TestWitherbloomOwnAffinityForCreatures`\n\nTests that `cost_reduction(game)` correctly implements affinity for creatures on\nWitherbloom itself. The oracle text states: \"This spell costs {1} less to cast for\neach creature you control.\"\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|---|---|\n| `test_zero_when_controller_has_no_creatures` | 0 creatures → reduction 0 |\n| `test_one_creature_gives_reduction_of_one` | 1 creature → reduction 1 |\n| `test_three_creatures_give_reduction_of_three` | 3 creatures → reduction 3 |\n| `test_witherbloom_itself_on_battlefield_counts_as_creature` | Witherbloom counts itself if already on board (second copy scenario, or checking from another source) |\n| `test_opponent_creatures_not_counted` | Only controller's creatures count, not opponent's |\n| `test_no_controller_returns_zero` | `controller=None` → returns 0 without raising |\n| `test_cost_reduction_does_not_count_non_creature_permanents` | Enchantments/non-creatures don't count |\n| `test_large_creature_count_returns_correct_value` | 6 creatures → reduction 6 |\n\n**Edge cases NOT covered here:** Tokens (they are creatures and would count, but this is\nstandard creature behavior — no separate test needed). Opponent's creatures mixed with\ncontroller's (covered by the opponent test).\n\n---\n\n### Class: `TestWitherbloomGrantsAffinityToSpells`\n\nTests the third ability: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for\ncreatures.\" The implementation is expected to expose `get_affinity_cost_reduction(spell, game)`\nthat parallels the `get_miracle_cost` / `get_casualty_value` patterns in the codebase.\n\n| Test | Requirement validated |\n|---|---|\n| `test_has_grants_method` | Method `get_affinity_cost_reduction` exists on the class |\n| `test_grants_method_is_callable` | It is callable |\n| `test_instant_gets_affinity_reduction_equal_to_creature_count` | Instant controlled by p1 gets reduction = number of p1's creatures |\n| `test_sorcery_gets_affinity_reduction_equal_to_creature_count` | Sorcery gets the same treatment |\n| `test_instant_gets_zero_reduction_when_no_creatures` | When p1 controls 0 creatures the grant returns 0 |\n| `test_creature_card_does_not_get_granted_affinity` | The grant only applies to instants/sorceries, not creatures |\n| `test_opponent_instant_does_not_get_granted_affinity` | Opponent-controlled instants are not affected |\n| `test_uncontrolled_witherbloom_returns_zero_for_grants` | `controller=None` → 0 without crash |\n| `test_granted_affinity_counts_only_controller_creatures` | When both players have creatures, only controller's count |\n\n**Why this method name:** The project follows a naming pattern of `get_X` for\n\"what X does this permanent grant to spell Y\" — e.g. `get_miracle_cost`, `get_casualty_value`.\n`get_affinity_cost_reduction(spell, game)` follows that pattern and returns an `int`\ncost reduction analogous to how `cost_reduction(game)` works on the card itself.\n\n**Edge cases NOT covered:**\n- Integration with the casting pipeline (where `get_affinity_cost_reduction` would\n  actually be called): this is engine territory and is exercised transitively when\n  the implementer wires up the casting hook. The contract tested here is sufficient\n  for TDD red-phase: the method must exist and return the right number.\n- The \"grant\" being removed when Witherbloom leaves the battlefield: this would\n  require a full combat/removal flow and is beyond single-card test scope.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3993,"cache_read_input_tokens":49058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3993,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018q5NbrHbQicM8zsL37LECz","session_id":"eab38cf5-7da5-43e8-ba85-a59c2942584c","uuid":"ce55fae4-d9db-4a97-af30-809376c7a130","request_id":"req_011CbUgRR59dNTQCYPSdXGsN","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Tester for sos_245"}
